  "whatIsThis": {
    "intro": "The flight controller is the drone's onboard computer. It runs Betaflight on an RP2354 (Raspberry Pi) and reads a 6-axis IMU to keep the drone stable and follow your sticks. It logs blackbox to a microSD card, draws an OSD on analog video, sends OSD data to digital video systems, and has a switchable 10 V output to power your VTX.",
    "needs": [
      "A 4-in-1 ESC and four motors (OpenESC pairs directly, one plug)",
      "A receiver wired to a UART (OpenRX, CRSF)",
      "A camera and VTX if you want a live video feed",
      "A frame, props, and a LiPo battery: 3-6S for the 20×20, 3-8S for the 30×30",
      "A radio and goggles on your side of the link"
    ],
    "fit": "It sits in the middle of the stack. The receiver, ESC, camera and VTX all connect to it.",
    "chain": "fc"
  },
